I played an elf ranger once who completed the Orion-Scorpius-
Long-Bow-Of-Diana quest.  I did it by stocking up on potions
of healing, because I'd been sickened-to-death by Scorpius
before.

Same trick works deeper in the dungeon on that swamp
level infested by that demon-of-sickness (I forget his name)
who ingests and sickens you.

In either case, drink potions of healing (potions of
"Full Healing" are best, if avail, but "extra healing"
will work also) every few moves, in between whacking
your opponent with your most potent available weapon.
Good armor class also helps with the non-sickness part
of your foe's attack.  Once you've killed your opponent,
if you're still sick, keep quaffing potions until you're
well.  (It's disheartening to successfully kill your foe,
only get: "You die from your illness.  DYWYPI?")

